<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mallu Adil Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1534">1534</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mallu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> was the third sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-adil-shah">Ismail Adil Shah</a> in 1534. His brief reign ended within months when he was deposed and blinded by nobles who placed his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-adil-shah-i">Ibrahim Adil Shah I</a> on the throne. He is remembered chiefly as an example of the factional politics that repeatedly shaped the Adil Shahi succession.</p></div>
